# The functions path is listed first so it is never swallowed by the catch-all.
/api/*        /.netlify/functions/:splat   200

# SPA routes. Each real route is listed explicitly and served with a 200,
# because these pages exist — they are just rendered by the app rather than
# sitting on disk as files.
/                 /index.html   200
/story            /index.html   200
/quote            /index.html   200
/privacy-policy   /index.html   200
/cookie-policy    /index.html   200
/terms            /index.html   200

# Everything else is genuinely not found, and must say so with a 404 status.
#
# This used to be `/*  /index.html  200`, which served the home page for every
# mistyped or dead URL and called it a success. That is a "soft 404": Google
# treats it as a duplicate of the home page rather than a missing one, which
# wastes crawl budget and can suppress the real pages in search results — and a
# link checker, an uptime monitor or a browser can never tell a typo from a
# working page. The app still renders (same shell), it just renders the
# not-found route with an honest status code behind it.
/*                /index.html   404
